Room: the video picture-in-picture window's controls drawn by //room.

The user asked for Dia's look on the floating video (5.12), then for
AppKit's own Liquid Glass controls (5.13). VideoOverlayWindowViews builds
and lays out its views itself with no seam for an embedder, so two calls
hand them to //room: once the views exist and after each layout. Since
5.13 //room hides Chrome's controls and scrims and puts AppKit glass
controls over the video in the window's content view; they act through
the window's controller. Two accessors give //room the session's position
and whether it is live, which Chrome's controls read from private members.

Phase 5.12, 2026-11-01; 5.13, 2026-11-02. //room: room/browser/room_video_overlay.mm.
